[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Consequence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `void driver(int x)` is a `void` function that takes a single by-value `int`. It
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m performs **no** validation of any kind:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no error-return macro or `return <sentinel>` statement — it cannot return a value at all;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no `assert`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no explicit range check, no min/max constant;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no null check — it accepts no pointer, so a null pointer is not a representable input;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no error enum, and no enum parameter — so there is no out-of-range-enum input either;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no `errno` use, no `exit`/`abort`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the only conditional in the file is the loop guard `i < len` in `print_hex`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and `len` is a compile-time `sizeof(x)` == 4, never attacker-controlled.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every one of the 2^32 values of `x` is therefore a **valid** input with defined
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m output. The error surface is genuinely EMPTY, and the rows below record that
